From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takashi Nakayama <tnak@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:02:02 -0700
Subject: ServiceWorker: Drop ServiceWorkerMainResourceHandle for CSP-sandboxed
 workers

When shared and dedicated worker scripts are received and started, its
PolicyContainerPolicies must be computed and checked to prevent invalid
ServiceWorker from running for the shared/dedicated worker.

This CL ensures the calculation of PolicyContainerPolicies in
DidCreateScriptLoader() and drops ServiceWorkerHandle if the worker is
sandboxed by CSP.

See the bug for details.

Bug: 41478971, 563194341
Change-Id: I8e1df63ea670b10a3bfec73dedd47036ae62dd5e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8461264
Reviewed-by: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Yoshisato Yanagisawa <yyanagisawa@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Takashi Nakayama <tnak@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1712040}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
- worker_script_fetcher.cc: this branch predates the
  GetConnectionAllowlistsForWorker() helper (connection_allowlist_utils),
  so ComputePolicyContainerPoliciesForWorker() inlines the branch's
  existing connection-allowlist selection logic (same conditions, now
  copying instead of moving from the const creator policies) and still
  assigns the result to policies.connection_allowlists unconditionally,
  as upstream does. base/types/optional_util.h is included explicitly
  for base::OptionalToPtr().
- dedicated_worker_host.cc: DidStartScriptLoad() on this branch does not
  build a PolicyContainerHost (that came with the later connection
  allowlist work), so the CSP-sandbox check reads
  result->policy_container_policies.sandbox_flags directly, before the
  policies are moved into CommitResponseAndRelease().
- shared_worker_host.cc: the EnsureRequiredHeadersForIsolatedApp()
  context block does not exist on this branch; only the feature-gated
  policies selection was applied.
- dedicated_worker_service_impl_unittest.cc hunks were dropped (test-only,
  heavy context drift; the friend declaration in the header is kept).

